        "helpContent": {
            "ALG_DESC": "This model computes the Land Suitability for CSP systems in ECOWAS region.", 
            "ALG_HELP_CREATOR": "Giacomo Delli \nSE4ALL EU-TAF expert \nThe EU 's Technical Assistance Facility (TAF) \nfor the Sustainable Energy for All (SE4ALL) initiative Central and Western Africa", 
            "roads": "Road network, as provided by WAPP.\nFile: groads_ecowas.shp. \nThe field FCLASS is used for unselecting Trails\n", 
            "rclrulesroads": "File: ClassificationRules\\2_LandSuitability\\ReclassDistanceRoads_CSP.txt", 
            "rclrulesecowpop": "File: ClassificationRules\\2_LandSuitability\\ReclassPopulationDensity_CSP.txt", 
            "rclrulesghi": "File: ClassificationRules\\2_LandSuitability\\ReclassDNI.txt", 
            "ecowpop": "Population Density, as provided by ECREEE \nFile: ecreee_ecowpop.tif", 
            "MASKED_ALGSAGAGRIDMASKING_2": "Geographical Potential for CSP systems, based on the presently existing transmission lines + planned lines up to 2020\n\nEquation: \u01a9 (FactorClass * FactorWeight)\n\nWeights are those used by the Univerisity of Geneva. They can be computed with the Spreadsheet AHP_GeogrPot.xlsx, using a simplified version of the Analytical Hierarchy Process.\n", 
            "MASKED_ALGSAGAGRIDMASKING_3": "Geographical Potential for CSP systems, based on the presently existing transmission lines + planned lines up to 2030\n\nEquation: \u01a9 (FactorClass * FactorWeight)\n\nWeights are those used by the Univerisity of Geneva. They can be computed with the Spreadsheet AHP_GeogrPot.xlsx, using a simplified version of the Analytical Hierarchy Process.\n", 
            "rcldistsettlements": "File: ClassificationRules\\2_LandSuitability\\ReclassDistanceSettlements.txt", 
            "MASKED_ALGSAGAGRIDMASKING_1": "Geographical Potential for CSP systems, based on the presently existing transmission lines.\n\nEquation: \u01a9 (FactorClass * FactorWeight)\n\nWeights are those used by the Univerisity of Geneva. They can be computed with the Spreadsheet AHP_GeogrPot.xlsx, using a simplified version of the Analytical Hierarchy Process.\n", 
            "rcllandcoverurban": "File: ClassificationRules\\2_LandSuitability\\ReclassLandCover_Urban.txt", 
            "exclusionmaskpvongrid": "Exclusion Areas for CSP systems.\nRaster File, output from Module 1.3", 
            "ALG_VERSION": "2.0", 
            "landcover": "Land Cover layer, as downloaded from https://www.iscgm.org/gmd/ \nFile: gm_lc_v3.tif", 
            "rclpopdens500": "File: ClassificationRules\\2_LandSuitability\\ReclassPopulationDensity_Above500.txt", 
            "rcldistancegridlines": "File: ClassificationRules\\2_LandSuitabilityl\\ReclassDistanceGridLines_CSP.txt", 
            "OUTPUT_ALGGDALOGRTRANSLATE_1": "Land Suitability for CSP systems, based on the presently existing transmission lines\n\nEquation: \u01a9 (FactorClass * FactorWeight)\n\nWeights are those used by the Univerisity of Geneva. They can be computed with the Spreadsheet AHP_GeogrPot.xlsx, using a simplified version of the Analytical Hierarchy Process.\n", 
            "OUTPUT_ALGGDALOGRTRANSLATE_3": "Land Suitability for CSP systems, based on the presently existing transmission lines + planned lines up to 2030\nEquation: \u01a9 (FactorClass * FactorWeight)\n\nWeights are those used by the Univerisity of Geneva. They can be computed with the Spreadsheet AHP_GeogrPot.xlsx, using a simplified version of the Analytical Hierarchy Process.\n", 
            "OUTPUT_ALGGDALOGRTRANSLATE_2": "Land Suitability for CSP systems, based on the presently existing transmission lines + planned lines up to 2020\n\nEquation: \u01a9 (FactorClass * FactorWeight)\n\nWeights are those used by the Univerisity of Geneva. They can be computed with the Spreadsheet AHP_GeogrPot.xlsx, using a simplified version of the Analytical Hierarchy Process.\n", 
            "ALG_CREATOR": "Giacomo Delli \nSE4ALL EU-TAF expert \nThe EU 's Technical Assistance Facility (TAF) \nfor the Sustainable Energy for All (SE4ALL) initiative Central and Western Africa", 
            "transmissionlines": "TransmissionLines.shp, lines, as provided by WAPP.\nThe fields Voltage, Situation and Year are used to select relevant grid lines for present situation, for Year 2020 and for Year 2030.\n", 
            "referencegrid1km": "Reference Grid for all layers, resolution: 1 km\nRaster File: ReferenceGrid1000.tif\n", 
            "wdpawa": "WDPA_July2016_wa.shp. \nSource file (WDPA_July2016-shapefile.zip) was downloaded from http://www.protectedplanet.net/ , then clipped in ArcGIS on the boundaries of Ecowas region", 
            "ghi": "Direct Normal Irradiance  in kWh/m2/year\nFile: dni_ecowas.tif, output from module 2.1"
        }, 
        "group": "2. Land Suitability", 
